<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caravaggio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1571–1610</span> · Also known as Michelangelo Merisi da Caravaggio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caravaggio, born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> Merisi, was an Italian painter whose dramatic realism and strong contrasts of light and shadow transformed European painting around 1600. Working in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from the 1590s, he painted works such as The Calling of Saint Matthew. After killing a man in 1606 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, and he died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-ercole">Porto Ercole</a> in 1610.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caravaggio.jpg" alt="Caravaggio" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ottavio Leoni · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bild-Ottavio_Leoni,_Caravaggio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
